# 4. Access the app
Via Ingress:

http://react-app.local
Via port-forward (quick test):

kubectl port-forward svc/react-app 8080:80

# open http://localhost:8080

🧪 Verify the SPA Routing Works
This is the most common gotcha for React apps. Test it:

# Should return index.html (SPA fallback)
curl -I http://localhost:8080/some/deep/route

# Should return HTTP 200, not 404
Your nginx.conf already handles this with try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html; ✅

🔄 Updating Your App
When you change the React code:

bash
docker build -t YOUR_DOCKERHUB_USERNAME/react-app:v2 .
docker push YOUR_DOCKERHUB_USERNAME/react-app:v2

# edit deployment.yaml image tag to :v2
kubectl apply -f k8s/deployment.yaml
kubectl rollout status deployment react-app
Kubernetes performs a rolling update — old Pods are replaced gradually, no downtime.

Rollback if needed:

kubectl rollout undo deployment react-app